label start:

    scene black
    with fade 

    pause 2.0

    me "I used to think growng up meant forgetting things."
    me "The names of people you went to school with."
    me "The way your childhood home smelled after it rained."
    me "The exact sound of your mother's footsteps coming down the hall."
    me "I thought forgetting was something that happened to you."
    me "I didn't know you could do it on purpose."
    me "I forget June first."
    me "Or maybe I just got better at pretending."
    scene bg bedroom
    with dissolve
    me "The envelope was sitting outside my apartment."
    me "No return address.. my name written in blue ink."
    me "I recognized the handwriting before I touched it."
    me "That's the stupid part."
    me "I hadn't seen that handwriting in eleven years."
    me "(Happy, birthday, idiot.)"
    me "(You said you'd come this time.)"
    me "(I'm still waiting.)"
    me "(Saturday, six o'clock.)"
    me "(Don't bring a present, just make sure you're there.)"
    me "(Love, June.)"
    me "There was no year written on it."
    me "June had always hated writing the year on birthday invitations."
    me "He said it made birthdays sound like counting the days until you die."
    me "When we were twelve, he told me that when we turned eighteen, we'd run away together."
    me "I asked him where we'd go."
    me "He said somewhere nobody knew our names."
    me "I told him that was a terrible plan."
    me "He said that I was a terrible person."
    me "We were bestfriends."
    me "I never went to his eighteenth birthday."
    menu:
        "Keep the letter":
            $ kept_the_letter = True 
            me "I folded it carefully and put it in my drawer."

        "Throw it away.":
            me "I tore it into half."
            me "Then into quarters."
            me "Then into pieces so small, I couldn't read my own name."
            me "I threw everything into the bin."

    scene black
    with fade

    me "Saturday came."
    me "I almost didn't go."
    me "I told myself a lot of things."
    me "None of theme were the reason I was afraid."

    scene bg road
    with dissolve

    me "The road to June's house hadn't changed."
    me "The same tree where we used to hang our school bags."
    me "Everything was smaller than I remembered."
    me "Except the distance."
    me "The walk used to take five minutes."
    me "I walked for forty."
    me "I checked my phone."
    me "6:04 PM."
    me "One missed call."
    me "From June."
    me "The call was dated 11 years ago."
    me "I deleted it."
    me "Then I stood there for a while, staring at the empty screen."
    me "I wanted it to ring again."
    me "That was the first terrible thing I did that evening."

    scene bg house
    with dissolve

    me "The front gate was open."
    me "The paint had peeled away from the walls."
    me "The garden had grown wild."
    me "Someone had pulled the curtains shut from the inside."
    me "I remembered June's mother planting flowers here."
    me "June told me her mother could make anything grow."
    me "Even things that didn't want to."
    me "I stood at the gate."
    me "I could still turn around."
    me "I could go home, lock the door, and spend another eleven years pretending that I hadn't recieved the invitation."
    me "I could be sensible."
    me "I could be safe."
    me "But I had spent eleven years being safe."
    me "And I was so tired of it."

    play sound "door_creak.ogg"

    me "The front door was unlocked."

    scene bg livingroom
    with dissolve

    me "The smell hit me first, something sweet."
    me "Vanila.. birthday cake."
    me "That was impossible, I knew the house had been empty for years."
    me "I'd read the news, driven past it once and kept driving."
    me "I'd prove everything a person could prove they didn't care."
    me "Apparently, none of it had worked."
    me "There were photographs on the wall."
    me "June with a missing front tooth."
    me "June with a missing front tooth."
    me "June holding a frog."
    me "June asleep on my shoulder during a school trip."
    me "And one of us at twelve."
    me "We were standing in front of this house."
    me "I was smiling."

    return